7] [17592186289208 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b1d93a8c-2868-5548-992e-86797465c0a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289259 #edb/ref 1080 "An arc of a downward-opening parabola, traversed from $(2,1)$ to $(1,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289259 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289259 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ba18cd8c-2285-5486-8226-bfb496f3b81a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289281 #edb/ref 1080 "$(2,-1)$ and $(0,0)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289281 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289281 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bdbf2fce-7275-51db-ae2f-706d92628bd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289798 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289798 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289798 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186288933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289798 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1cb1a6c5-6f69-563f-88b4-ffb836efd328" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289928 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289928 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289928 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289928 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186288347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289928 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5cf66fd9-3498-5637-8fc1-454524321dda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290210 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290210 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290210 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186289112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290210 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e191ff6e-214b-558e-9919-97349fa4da47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290419 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290419 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225122" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290419 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290419 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3}(v+6u),\\,y=\\frac{{v}^{3}-2u}{v+2}.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{1}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290419 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "13002a7e-2ad6-501a-b8db-7a8abc685d5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290419 #edb/ref 1074 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{1}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{1},$ we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}(v+6u),\\,\\frac{{v}^{3}-2u}{v+2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}(0+6u),\\,\\frac{{0}^{3}-2u}{0+2}) \\\\  & =(2u,-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{1}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2u,\\,y=-u,\\,0\\le u\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2t,\\,y(t)=-t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(0,0)$ and $(2,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](images/f0/f068883d1318acdafba39c74bc1279f6cafe803437a9b79249999df461bac8ee.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373896 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373896 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373896 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373896 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373896 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373896 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373896 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373896 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186373897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373896 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "419acef2-b0e8-560d-bfb9-5d30aad77e63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373897 #edb/ref 1080 "An arc of a right-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,0)$ to $(2,-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373897 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373897 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6cc68d80-39d1-5f0f-933c-89bd1b4b4d27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373898 #edb/ref 1080 "An arc of an upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,1)$ to $(2,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373898 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373898 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b20916f4-2125-5e54-be30-7b22ca6d6f51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373899 #edb/ref 1080 "An arc of an upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(2,-1)$ to $(1,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373899 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373899 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f69006ab-7ec1-5771-bd33-a19fe8da912c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373900 #edb/ref 1080 "An arc of a right-opening parabola, traversed from $(2,-1)$ to $(1,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373900 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373900 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d3fa41a-6316-5747-87cf-e13860d909ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373901 #edb/ref 1080 "An arc of an upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,0)$ to $(2,-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373901 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373901 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "732254b6-7d89-598e-b5b3-79f480fa4f76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373902 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373902 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160636" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373902 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373902 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/5f/5f91cc8b30f9b764021cd84c374a328c7ffb1287a9f0dc6a211a3fadfac2fdbd.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=u{v}^{2},\\,y={u}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind the image of $Δ$ under the action of $T.$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373902 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4de9b2d-c42a-5fe3-94b3-1b2caac795c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373902 #edb/ref 1074 "We're told that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$ So, to map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we transform each side of $Δ$ separately:\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{1},$ where we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u({0}^{2}),\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(0,\\,{u}^{2}), & 0\\le u\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a vertical line segment traversed from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(0,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{2}.$ Here, we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(1{v}^{2},\\,{1}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =({v}^{2},\\,1), & 0\\le v\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment traversed from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{3}.$ Here, we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u({1}^{2}),\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u,\\,{u}^{2}), & 1\\ge u\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is an upward-opening parabola traversed from the point $(1,1)$ to the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{4}.$ Here, we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(0{v}^{2},\\,{0}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(0,\\,0), & 1\\ge v\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThis is the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nDrawing the images of the sides of our square, we obtain the following image of $Δ:$\n\n![](images/64/648fa48df1bd648d9fbf48efc966698228416ad9bf3a0f69045031e955601d61.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373903 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373903 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373905 #edb/ref 1